issue.body:
When `frappe.ui.FileUploader` is mounted in a custom `wrapper` (e.g. inside a `frappe.ui.Dialog`), the inline **Upload file** button that appears after choosing a file:

- sits right against the file preview card, with no space above it
- is pushed in from the right edge, so it doesn't line up with the card or the dialog's close button

<img width="576" height="220" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c2240c8c-67dd-4279-bc67-8703f8c862a3" />

### Steps to reproduce

Run in the browser console, then pick any file from **My Device**:

```js
const d = new frappe.ui.Dialog({
	title: "Choose File",
	fields: [{ fieldtype: "HTML", fieldname: "uploader" }],
});
frappe.require("file_uploader.bundle.js", () => {
	new frappe.ui.FileUploader({ wrapper: d.fields_dict.uploader.$wrapper });
	d.show();
});
```

### Cause and possible fix

In `FileUploader.vue`, the button row has no top margin and the button has a `margin-right` class. Adding `mt-3` to the row and removing `margin-right` should fix it.

**Frappe:** v16.34.0

